WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.240
What made Emily Blunt cry on the set of Edge of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.960
Tomorrow — and what was up with&nbsp;
Tom Cruise's brutal response?

00:00:07.302 --> 00:00:09.509
"This is where I come to cry"

00:00:10.067 --> 00:00:14.760
The 2014 action epic Edge of Tomorrow may&nbsp;
have been one of the best sci-fi movies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:19.080
of the last decade, but it's one that&nbsp;
star Emily Blunt might want to forget.

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:24.120
Set around Blunt and Hollywood legend Tom&nbsp;
Cruise's futuristic soldiers, Edge of Tomorrow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:30.180
is a time-loop tale about fate and redemption,&nbsp;
one which sees humanity waging a war against an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:36.060
alien super-organism known as the Omega. During&nbsp;
the opening battle, however, Cruise's character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:41.040
manages to kill one of the Omega's drones and&nbsp;
somehow co-opts their ability to loop time.

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:46.080
In order to defeat the movie's alien invaders,&nbsp;
Edge of Tomorrow's human soldiers are equipped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:50.700
with armored ExoSuits, which were built from&nbsp;
scratch by director Doug Liman's production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.520
team and weighed nearly 100 pounds. According&nbsp;
to Blunt, filming Edge of Tomorrow inside the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.520 --> 00:01:02.040
super-heavy ExoSuits was one of the most grueling&nbsp;
tasks she's ever faced in Hollywood — to the point&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:06.240
where she broke down crying in front of Tom&nbsp;
Cruise on the very first day of test shoots.

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:07.620
"And?"

00:01:09.476 --> 00:01:13.637
"It's a cold hard world, s--t happens."

00:01:14.456 --> 00:01:17.500
On an episode of the&nbsp;
"SmartLess" podcast, she said:

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.580
"The first time I put it&nbsp;
on, I just started to cry,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:24.241
started to cry, in front of Tom,&nbsp;
and he didn't know what to do."

00:01:24.241 --> 00:01:29.400
Production designer Oliver Scholl and costume&nbsp;
designer Kate Hawley were responsible for creating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:34.920
the ExoSuits. Doug Liman wanted a "simplified&nbsp;
and raw" look to them, and a team of handlers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:39.900
had to be used to get the suits on each actor&nbsp;
every day. For Cruise, specifically, it took&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:46.200
around 30 minutes just to get inside his suit when&nbsp;
testing first started — and another 30 minutes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.200 --> 00:01:51.201
get out. By the time the shoot began, though,&nbsp;
Cruise had cut the time down to 30 seconds.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:53.040
"Where's your helmet?"

00:01:55.073 --> 00:01:56.753
"Never wear one."

00:01:56.753 --> 00:02:00.180
While the actor viewed the ExoSuits&nbsp;
as an on-set challenge, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.180 --> 00:02:04.440
Blunt saw them more as an unbearable&nbsp;
nuisance, which prompted Cruise to give&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.520
her some harsh advice. When it came time&nbsp;
for Blunt to begin test shoots with Tom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:12.720
Cruise — and the tears started flowing&nbsp;
— Cruise apparently didn't hold back.

00:02:13.034 --> 00:02:15.360
"He stared at me for a long&nbsp;
time, not knowing what to do,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:17.700
and he goes, 'Come on, stop&nbsp;
being such a p***y, okay?'"

00:02:17.939 --> 00:02:20.339
According to Blunt, the comment was laughed off,

00:02:20.339 --> 00:02:25.724
(Tom Cruise laughing)

00:02:25.724 --> 00:02:29.340
and things were reportedly fine between&nbsp;
the two actors throughout the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:33.153
shoot. But that didn't make things&nbsp;
any easier on Cruise's co-star.

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.220
"I had to do this aerial stunt on wires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:38.879
and I was supposed to land on my&nbsp;
shoulder, "And I landed on my face."

00:02:38.879 --> 00:02:43.740
Despite everything, Blunt was reportedly on&nbsp;
board to film an Edge of Tomorrow sequel in 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.834
but the plans were eventually scrapped.&nbsp;
